---
<Base title="Elections" description="How and when the Alabama Section elects its Section Coordinator.">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="page-head">
      <h1>Elections</h1>
      <p class="lede">The Section Coordinator is elected by the member clubs, one vote per club. USPSA requires an election at least every two years; the Alabama bylaws set a one-year term running 1 April to 31 March.</p>
    </div>
    <GovNav />

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Current status</h2>
      <p>Current Section Coordinator: Rodney Hawkins. Term dates and next election: <span class="soon">Coming soon</span>. Election notices are posted under <a href="/notices/">Notices</a>.</p>

      <h2>Who may serve</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Current USPSA membership (at least annual) throughout the term.</li>
        <li>NROI Range Officer (Level I) or higher certification.</li>
        <li>Policy §3.2. Losing either qualification vacates the office.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How the vote works</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Held at an Executive Committee meeting, normally the annual meeting at the Section Championship (Bylaws Art. 6, 7.D).</li>
        <li>One vote per member club, cast by the club president or their designated representative (Art. 5, 8). No one may represent more than one club.</li>
        <li>A majority of the committee is a quorum (Art. 6.B).</li>
        <li>The Section Coordinator serves until they resign, relinquish the office, a successor is elected, or the Area Director removes them for cause (Policy §3.3).</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Special elections and vacancies</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>A majority of club presidents may call a special election at any time (Policy §3.5(b)).</li>
        <li>If the office becomes vacant, the Area 6 Director appoints an interim Section Coordinator until an election is held (Policy §3.5(a); Bylaws Art. 7.D).</li>
        <li>A vacancy lasting more than 12 months without an appointment is grounds for dissolving the Section (Policy §8.1(d)). So is failing to hold required elections (§8.1(c)).</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Paperwork after an election</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Report the result to the Area 6 Director and the USPSA national office.</li>
        <li>Send USPSA the current bylaws (required at every election, Policy §2.6(b)).</li>
        <li>Transfer Section funds and records to the incoming Section Coordinator by 15 January of the new term (Bylaws Art. 7.E).</li>
        <li>Update the <a href="/governance/">officers table</a> on this site and post a notice.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
